# Per-call scratch directories for the anvil hazard harness's deploys
# (tools/goat-attestor/src/stream_g/anvil_harness.rs::ScratchDeploymentsDir).
# They live under deployments/ because foundry.toml's fs_permissions grant
# `vm.writeJson` write access to that subtree and nowhere else, and they are
# removed on drop; this entry only covers a run killed mid-deploy.
deployments/.harness-*/

# Per-test scratch directories for the same reason one level in: forge runs a
# contract's test functions concurrently, so DeployStreamGTest's payload test
# publishes into its own directory instead of racing
# test_writes_only_31337_stream_g_json on the committed
# deployments/31337.stream-g{,.payload}.json pair (vm.writeJson truncates before
# it writes). That one test keeps the committed pair as its output because
# regenerating it on every `forge test` is what makes a contract edit surface as
# a byte-identity failure against tools/goat-attestor/fixtures/.
#
# The name carries a millisecond timestamp and a random suffix because
# `forge test` is not one process: two concurrent runs (a terminal and
# run-full-gate.ps1 step 4) used to share one fixed path, and each one DELETED
# it recursively on entry -- so one run's vm.writeJson landed while the other
# was between its removeDir and its createDir (`os error 3`). Removed by a
# passing run, kept by a failing one so the documents can be inspected. See
# _scratchDeploymentsDir in test/DeployStreamG.t.sol.
deployments/.streamg-t-*/
